 7. 📉 Death penalty support crumbles 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Gallup. Chart: Avery Lotz/Axios For the first time since 1971, fewer than half of Americans support the death penalty for convicted murderers, Axios' Avery Lotz writes from a new Gallup poll . 

 Gallup started its most recent polling on the question a day after death row inmate Christa Pike survived a botched lethal injection process in Tennessee, triggering a pause on executions in the state. Go deeper . 

 
 
