 8. ✈️ 1 for the road: United&#x27;s bot ban 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Shoshana Gordon/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 United Airlines is blocking personal AI assistants like Meta's Muse and OpenAI's Dots from accessing its systems to book tickets, The Wall Street Journal reports . 

 The airline cited concerns about sensitive customer information, unintended purchases and potential violations of federal aviation rules. AI agents can still show customers United's flight options and prices but won't be allowed to book tickets directly on its website.

